## Tools

`config/toolchain.json` pins every tool this project downloads: URL, sha256,
version, license and where the bytes came from. `configure.py` fetches them into
`build/tools/` with `tools/download_tool.py` (standard library only), checking the
sha256 before anything is extracted or run. romwright itself downloads nothing.

* The assembler, linker and objcopy are GNU binutils 2.40 (GPL) from decompals'
  release, which accepts `-EB`/`-EL` and the MIPS ISA levels these platforms use.
* The compilers are proprietary or third-party builds of unverified provenance
  (IDO, PSY-Q, Metrowerks) or GPL builds (gcc). They are fetched from the release
  assets the decomp.me compilers images use; use them only if you are entitled to.
  Nothing in this repository grants that right.
* To use tools you already have, write a toolchain profile (JSON, the format in
  romwright's `docs/toolchains.md`) and pass `python3 configure.py --toolchain profile.json`,
  or save it as `config/toolchain.local.json` (ignored by git).
* `--manifest FILE` substitutes another manifest, e.g. one whose URLs are
  `file://` copies for an offline machine.

## Decompiling a function

Every function is its own `asm/<segment>/NNNN/<name>.s` ({{ASM_UNITS}} of them). To replace one
with C:

```sh
python3 configure.py swap <name-or-0xADDRESS> [--src my_function.c]
# edit src/<segment>/NNNN/<name>.c until `ninja` is green again
ninja progress                               # objdiff report (build/report.json)
```

`romwright-cli match <name-or-0xADDRESS> [--write]` run in this directory tries alternative
printings of the function with this project's compiler and flags and keeps the closest.

